1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:14,980
[upbeat music]

2
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:24,100
Look at me. I've never done this before.
I want to try it and see what happens.

3
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:28,960
And, you know, games and computers
never get old. [clears throat]

4
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:34,820
So I can see myself on the computer
for a long time, always...

5
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:37,960
at the same age. I can get older,
but the computer never does.

6
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:42,530
So I think I'd better
preserve my moves.

7
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:46,670
What I can do today,
I might not be able to do in ten years.

8
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:51,500
I need to preserve my moves,
my acting and my humor. Put it all

9
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:55,339
in the computer. One day,
it becomes a memory.

10
00:00:55,840 --> 00:01:00,780
It's a game. They show it to people,
let children play it, and can also

11
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:03,780
keep that memory
for myself.

12
00:01:04,190 --> 00:01:10,860
[upbeat music]

13
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,300
It's completely different from movies.

14
00:01:13,460 --> 00:01:19,240
They ask me to do something
with nobody around,

15
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:24,900
acting on my own. You have to
pretend you're a helicopter.

16
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:27,160
You have to pretend the truck's
coming. You do this...

17
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:29,520
Usually we do things
for real, you know?

18
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:32,700
The truck comes, boom!
You really get hit...

19
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:35,080
Now you act with nothing there.

20
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:39,160
You act just for the computer.
But I find it very interesting.

21
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:46,110
[upbeat music]

22
00:01:46,630 --> 00:01:51,220
I play video games because they
give me lots of ideas and keep

23
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:54,800
my mind active. But nowadays,
games are harder.

24
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:56,900
It's not like ten or fifteen years ago.

25
00:01:56,980 --> 00:01:59,480
It was simple: two buttons.
Now there are too many buttons.

26
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:01,680
Wow, it really keeps you busy!

27
00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:08,540
[upbeat music]

28
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:11,340
They scan me about
every five hours.

29
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:17,720
I think that's good. Why?
Because afterward my face stays

30
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:20,300
the same age forever.
I hope so.

31
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:29,880
[upbeat music]

32
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:34,800
I want to add more humor.
It's not just about fighting.

33
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:38,420
Humor and comedy
are the most important things.

34
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:44,560
I don't like violence. But there's
a big dilemma between violence and action.

35
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:48,180
Everyone thinks action is violence,
but look at my movies.

36
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:52,520
I like action, so I put in
as little violence as possible.

37
00:02:52,620 --> 00:02:57,520
Even in the game, I ask them to add
more comedy, to show my jumps

38
00:02:57,840 --> 00:03:03,420
and kicks. Then children can
learn from the jumps, spins, kicks

39
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:06,780
and punches, you know?
It's like exercise.

40
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:12,960
[upbeat music]

41
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:18,200
Nowadays, in American movies, there are
lots of explosions and gunfights.

42
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:23,960
So I tell myself: "No explosions,
no gunfire." I want something different

43
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:28,280
from other action stars.
When blood comes out of the nose

44
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:33,360
or mouth, fine. But in my movies,
there's no blood. Even after all the hits,

45
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:36,680
people get up
without bruises or anything.

46
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:42,440
I want to be like a comic book.
That's why I fight with a ladder,

47
00:03:43,180 --> 00:03:47,160
a staff, anything. But in the US,
a lot of directors ask me:

48
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:50,540
"How can you do that?
How can you fight with a ladder?

49
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:52,700
How can you jump
over a building?

50
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:56,340
How do you do all the choreography,
all the fight scenes?"

51
00:03:56,820 --> 00:04:01,120
To me, those things are easy.
I think it's a different world.

52
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:07,420
[upbeat music]

53
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:23,340
Me?

54
00:04:24,460 --> 00:04:25,460
Jackie.

55
00:04:27,219 --> 00:04:41,479
[upbeat music]

56
00:04:41,690 --> 00:04:44,000
[graphic transition sound effect]
